--- Report - QA using MongoDB ---
=================================

Data Loading
------------
	* Data from CSV, JSON, Parquet (after conversion), or API responses can be loaded into MongoDB collections.
	* Once loaded, data can be viewed on MongoDB Compass and queried using mongosh
	
Schema Analysis in MongoDB Compass
----------------------------------
	* MongoDB Compass provides a Schema Analysis feature that define a collection and generates statistics for each field.
	* It shows how frequently a field appears in documents.
	* Analyse and report datatypes observed in each field and it's percentage.
	* Schema analysis also reveals Null values, Missing values, Empty arrays, Empty objects
	* It displays frequency distribution of field values too.
	
Drawbacks
---------
	* Schema analysis displays report of only 1000 records in the dataset, which can be inferred as the report of the whole dataset.
	* Checking field order not possible in compass.
	* For business rules analysis, pattern validation etc. we need to use mongosh and learn querying, anyway it is powerful and effective method to analyse data.
	* For doing simple tasks like checking whether unique, null, finding distinct value etc. manual method using sublime is more productive.
	
Benefits
--------
	* Data count can be easily found using compass.
	* Reduces human errors.
	* If using mongosh and querying, the analysis process become more effective and productive.
